{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.criterion_trait`\n\n`Criterion::version` identifies the version of the review rules and the\ncompleted answer's encoding:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Criterion<D: Domain>: Send + Sized {\n    // ...\n\n    /// Version of these review rules and the result's encoding.\n    /// Change it when an old answer should no longer be reused.\n    fn version(&self) -> CriterionVersion;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```\n\nThe {term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.source_node`,\n{term}`requirements.sdk.graph.criteria.question_path`, and version identify\nthe same question for checking and execution. Parameters that change which\nquestion is being asked belong in its identity or version.\n\n[Storage](evidence.md#identify-the-saved-assessment) explains how the source node\nand criterion path identify a saved answer and how its version is recorded.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `criterion_trait.version`**\n1. `Criterion::version` returns a `CriterionVersion` that identifies the review rules and the answer's encoding. A changed version means an old answer is not reused.\n2. The source node, the criterion path and the version together identify the same question for checking and execution.\n3. Parameters that change the question belong in the identity or the version.\n\n**Test coverage**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[caller_reuses_negative_answers_and_compares_revisions_explicitly]`\n  - The test `Review` criterion builds its version from its `revision` parameter, so a parameter that changes the question is carried in the version.\n  - A v1 answer is stored and reloaded. `review().version().is_compatible_with(cached.version())` holds for the same version.\n  - After a `v2` review is loaded, the stored version is `\"v1\"` and `!v2.version().is_compatible_with(old.version())` holds. This shows a changed version marks the old answer as not reusable.\n  - A replacement answer is then stored, and the saved record's version becomes `\"v2\"`.\n  - A different source node (8) loads no evidence, so the source node is part of the identity.\n  - A legacy record with no version is treated as compatible, and the test asserts that case.\n- `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_persists_and_reuses_a_negative_validation_through_the_sdk]`\n  - This test uses the real SDK `Review` criterion. It asserts `review().version().as_str() == REVIEW_VERSION`, so the version value is checked.\n  - The saved record's version is checked against `REVIEW_VERSION`.\n  - `source_node_id` and `criterion_path` are asserted.\n  - A different criterion path loads no record and its store is rejected, so the path is part of the identity.\n  - Reloaded evidence is version-compatible and reused. The provider is called once, which shows a cached answer is reused without re-executing.\n\n**Gaps**\nI found none. Each obligation, including the changed-version and identity-component cases, has a test with an assertion that enforces it. Nothing here is delegated to a refining requirement or exempted.",
